# FIX B — Visual sub-splitting on the CROP ONLY (no tagged_order change)
The Round 9/10 attempt failed because it renumbered tagged_order. This
time, do not touch the item list at all. Instead, enrich each placeholder
pdf item with a list of sub-crop OCR strings.

 1. Extend math_pdf_ocr_fill.py with:
      split_crop_and_ocr(pdf_item, crop_image, venv_python)
          -> list[str]
    Behavior:
      - Grayscale, Otsu threshold.
      - Row-wise ink profile, smoothed with 3-row box filter.
      - Dense bands: contiguous row ranges where profile > max(3, 0.10 *
        profile.max()).
      - Merge adjacent bands separated by < 3% of crop height.
      - If <= 1 band: return [pix2text(crop)].
      - If >= 2 bands AND item height > 1.5 * median_pdf_item_height for
        this file: for each band, crop rows [start-2, end+2], run
        Pix2Text, canonicalize, collect.
      - If > 6 bands: return [pix2text(crop)] (reject over-split).
      - Return the list in top-to-bottom order.
